# Product truth — describe HEALTHINGS.AI from the docs, never from memory

**You do not get to summarize this product from vibes.** The definition is written down. Read it,
quote it, link it. If a sentence about what Healthings *is* cannot be traced to a file below, do not
write that sentence.

Written 2026-08-25 after an outbound email to a supplier described the company as *"an innovative
startup aiming to disrupt metabolic care with advanced technologies: clinical protocols, continuous
measurement, and AI-guided nutrition."* The last clause is **false**, the email had already been sent
twice, and the correct wording was sitting in `website/index.html` the whole time.

## One line (source: `website/index.html`)

> **From lab report and nutritionist plan to today's targets.** Log meals and body trends; Healthings
> turns that loop into daily numbers and meal decisions **you confirm before they apply**.

Landing `<title>` calls it a **Metabolic OS**. The investor one-liner
(`investor-pov/EXECUTIVE-SUMMARY.md`) says it closes the loop between CGM, food log, smart scale and
blood labs — *"with human confirm, not black-box AI."*

## The loop

| Step | What happens |
|---|---|
| Import | Blood labs + the nutritionist's plan (PDF) |
| Log | Meals and weigh-ins — the app learns the body |
| Review | Daily targets — **user confirms before update** |
| Ask | AI mentors between visits, **on that plan** |
| Share | Weekly brief to the nutritionist / linked clinic |

## What it is **not**

- **Not "AI-guided nutrition."** Nutrition authority is the clinician's protocol, the imported
  directive, and My Rules. The model works **inside** those constraints and explains what moved
  (`ai-judgment-not-regex.mdc`). It does not set the diet.
- **Not autonomous.** Confirm-before-apply is a product promise, not an implementation detail. Never
  describe changes as applied automatically.
- **Not a medical device.** Alpha wellness app. No diagnosis, no prescribing, emergencies stay with
  licensed clinicians — the public pages say this out loud; so must you.
- **Not a CGM dashboard.** Charts are table stakes; the product sells the decision.
- **Not cloud-by-default.** Labs, meals, weight, glucose live **on the phone**. The server holds an
  email address plus whatever the user chooses to send. Clinic share and cloud backup are **opt-in
  and revocable**.

## Naming

| Context | Correct |
|---|---|
| Brand, outbound copy, signatures | **HEALTHINGS.AI** (caps, with `.AI`) |
| Running prose, help pages | Healthings |
| URL | `https://healthings.ai` |
| Repo / app package | `healthings-medilab`, "Healthings.ai Medilab" |

Never "Healthings AI", "Healthing", or the bare word "Medilab" to an outsider.

## Where the truth lives

| Question | File |
|---|---|
| Public product story, loop, privacy stance | `website/index.html` |
| Plain-language welcome, "not medical care" | `website/en/help/quick-start-welcome.html` |
| The clinic and who runs it | `website/en/the-clinic/index.html` |
| Positioning, competitors, honest weaknesses | `investor-pov/EXECUTIVE-SUMMARY.md`, `investor-pov/COMPETITOR-SCORES.md` |
| Who the user is, who is **not** the user | `investor-pov/key-rule.md`, `marketing/README.md` |
| What actually shipped | `prompts/app/*/done/`, `prompts/backend/done/` |
| How a behavior really works | the service in `app/src/services/` — e.g. `NutritionDirectiveService`, `TargetService`, `LabLogService`, `ClinicOverlayService`, `TreatmentMarkerService`, `GeminiService`, `CoachService` |

**When docs disagree, shipped code and `website/` win.** Root `readme.md` carries older framing
(AWS-centric, "MediLab") — treat it as history, not as the current pitch.

## Verify before quoting — these go stale

Platform gaps (live CGM on iOS), device support, pricing, user counts, market size, which clinics or
dietitians are live, and anything in `expenses/`. Open the file and check the date. An outdated number
in an outbound email is the same failure as an invented one.

